    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.starter\n\n### Description\n\nWith an existing starter buffer open, if I make a new tab for example and try to run `lua MiniStarter.open()` I get the following errors.\r\n\r\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua ...im/site/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/starter.lua:1240: Vim:E95: Buffer with this name already exists\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_buf_set_name'\r\n        ...im/site/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/starter.lua:1240: in function 'apply_buffer_options'\r\n        ...im/site/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/starter.lua:335: in function 'open'\r\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\r\n```\r\n```\r\nError detected while processing CursorMoved Autocommands for \"<buffer=4>\":\r\nE5108: Error executing lua ...im/site/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/starter.lua:1165: Cursor position outside buffer\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_win_set_cursor'\r\n        ...im/site/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/starter.lua:1165: in function 'position_cursor_on_current_item'\r\n        ...im/site/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/starter.lua:919: in function 'on_cursormoved'\r\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\r\n```\r\n\r\nMy ultimate goal is to have starter open when I create a new tab. I used to do this with alpha using:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.cmd([[ autocmd TabNewEntered * Alpha ]])\r\n```\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.7.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee Description.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSee Description.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nSee Description.",
